flowchart TB
  accTitle: Product X competing payment incident coalitions
  accDescr: The diagnostic coalition contains a pending ledger observation, a processor delay alert, and applicable idempotency evidence. The action coalition contains an unsupported retry proposal and plan fragment. In this teaching scenario the diagnostic coalition is admitted and broadcast to authorized read-only consumers. The broadcast does not authorize a payment retry; action authorization remains a separate control.
  subgraph D[Diagnostic evidence coalition]
    L[Pending ledger observation]
    A[Processor delay alert]
    I[Idempotency memory evidence]
  end
  subgraph R[Action-oriented coalition]
    P[Immediate retry proposal]
    F[Retry plan fragment]
  end
  D --> G[Bounded admission governor]
  R --> G
  G -->|admit diagnostic coalition| W[Cycle workspace snapshot]
  G -->|defer or reject| X[Non-admitted proposal remains outside]
  W --> B[Broadcast to authorized consumers]
  B --> C[Read-only status check and reasoning]
  C --> O[Outcome record]
  O --> U[Future policy evaluation]
  C -. separate authority .-> T[Action authorization gate]
  classDef source fill:#EAF4FB,stroke:#1A4A8A,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef process fill:#F4F4F4,stroke:#888888,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef output fill:#EEF7EE,stroke:#27AE60,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef caution fill:#FEF9E7,stroke:#F39C12,color:#1C1C1E
  class L,A,I source
  class P,F,X caution
  class G,W,B,C process
  class O,U output
